# Tracked so this directory EXISTS IN EVERY CHECKOUT.
#
# sbatch_powered_closure.sh sends --output/--error here. slurmstepd opens those paths before it
# execs the script, and SLURM does not create their parent directories, so the mkdir -p inside the
# script runs far too late. Job 56355818 was submitted with this directory absent: it would have
# held its queue slot and then died at dispatch with no log to say why. An empty tracked directory
# is a cheaper guard than remembering.
